==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|admissible}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[capable|Capable]] or [[deserving]] to be [[admitted]], [[accepted]] or [[allowed]]; [[allowable]], [[permissible]], [[acceptable]].
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=2018|author=James Lambert|title=Anglo-Indian slang in dictionaries on historical principles|journal=World Englishes|volume=37|page=255|text=Moreover, the term [...] is well recorded in British and Australian sources from the 1840s onwards, while the earliest Anglo-Indian evidence only extends as far back as 1865 and so does not hold precedence. Thus, deriving the term from Hindustani is not chronologically '''admissible''' on present evidence.}}
# {{lb|en|artificial intelligence}} Describing a [[heuristic]] that never [[overestimate]]s the [[cost]] of reaching a [[goal]].

